'' A generic instantiated DIRECTLY IN A TYPE FIELD, in both field spellings.
''
'' The layout is fbc's, measured 2026-09-19 on the all-'dim' spelling (the only one it
'' instantiates): sizeof( Holder ) = 40 with fields at 0, 8, 16 and 32, and
'' sizeof( Cell( of long ) ) = 8 with fields at 0 and 4.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/generic-type-field.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0

'' THE OUTER UDT IS SIZED BY ITS INSTANTIATIONS -- it used to be the whole point of the
'' feature that it was not: an instantiation that resolved to the generic's own fieldless
'' UDT makes every container field SIZE ZERO and the type around it collapses.
'' EXPECT-OUT: local agg h size 40
'' EXPECT-OUT: local agg c size 8

'' 'b as Box( of long )' -- the NAME-FIRST spelling, at offset 0, and the store goes
'' through the instantiation's own field, not through the generic's.
'' EXPECT-OUT: %3 = field.addr @h, 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: %4 = field.addr %3, 0

'' 'dim as Box( of double ) d' -- the TYPE-FIRST spelling, at 8.
'' EXPECT-OUT: %7 = field.addr @h, 8

'' 'pr as Pair( of long, double )' -- two arguments, name first, at 16; 'v' at 16+8.
'' EXPECT-OUT: %14 = field.addr @h, 16
'' EXPECT-OUT: %15 = field.addr %14, 8

'' The plain field AFTER the generic ones still lands where fbc puts it.
'' EXPECT-OUT: %17 = field.addr @h, 32
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' GOLDEN: expected/generic-type-field.out
